ious leader and  installing himself in a position of  power was sort of like putting a square  block  in a square hole now he's having  existentialist problems so  i guess somehow we've gone from  childhood to adolescence but the effect  is the same  he's having to deal with emotions he's  never had to deal with before and that  he was ill-equipped to deal with because  of how easily he was given everything  else  it's sort of a reproduction of three men  and a little lady except they're not all  men and he's a  super powerful entity but you get my  point meanwhile the other protagonists  are still preparing to break in and do  things as planned  despite not hearing from palm which is  very much a concern and should be a  concern for all of them  all of them they are doing a thing that  seems ill-advised given someone who  who knows the plan and and has powers  that can just watch them i don't know  i look at this ragtag bunch of oddballs  and think well if anyone can do  something about this you probably could  but i feel like  what you could do about it probably  isn't what you're intending to do about  it either way  it makes a good story so let's take a  look at episode 109  109 and mary's asking what do i want to  do with her  what indeed does he want her to be his  queen i think i raised something like  this before  the idea that maybe because he values  the strength of kamuki's strategic mind  he might elevate her but it seemed but  it's starting to seem like something  more  i don't know intense than that and she  seems to care just as much about him  in a way that i'm not sure how to  interpret the interesting thing about  this episode is that i was right in what  i said about the first one  as they all prepare to engage in  possibly the last moment in their lives  each of the characters get some  introspective time and i love that  because it tells us a lot about who they  are  the same as when we lost leol a few  episodes back while the rest of the  chara